<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices ease on poor demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices ease on poor demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Friday remained bearish, falling by 100-150 rupees on limited demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained bearish in thin trade as export demand was poor. Soymeal yellow was $278-281 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $104-105 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,550-3,600 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was easy.</p>
